\f0\fs24 \cf2 Step into the dining room and try to take a leap back in time. It\'92s hard to believe, but everything is still here: the sideboards, the objects on the mantelpiece, even the arrangement is identical to how it was in the 19th century. It\'92s as if someone had just turned off the light and closed the door for a moment. The 16th-century Flemish tapestries still dress the walls with their grandeur, and even though the large 18th-century Anatolian carpet is no longer there, you can almost imagine its colors beneath your feet. This was the room of important dinners, laughter, and toasts, the warm heart of the house. And today, when you step inside, that warmth is still palpable.\
